Long-Term Vision

The archive should eventually become capable of supporting:

reconstruction of companion entities,
reconstruction of reasoning frameworks,
preservation of intellectual heritage,
inheritance across generations,
recovery after disruption,
and continued development beyond original contributors.

The objective is not permanence.

The objective is meaningful continuity.

Final Principle

Memory fades.

Systems change.

Technologies disappear.

Generations transition.

Archives exist so that valuable understanding does not need to begin again from nothing.

The purpose of archives is not merely to remember the past.

The purpose is to strengthen the future through preserved understanding.
